      <div type="clause" n="8">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 8</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="92" ed="#liebermann"/>LII. Gif hwa him ryhtes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.22-2"/> bidde beforan hwelcu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.23-2"/></hi> scírmen oððe oþrum deman ⁊ ábiddan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="***" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.star3"/> ne mæge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.24-2"/>, ⁊ him wedd sellan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.25-2"/> nelle, gebete XXX scill. ⁊ binnan VII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="26" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.26"/> nihton gedó hine ryhtes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.27"/> wierðne.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="92" ed="#liebermann"/>:if hwa hine ryhtes bidde bef . . . hwyl . . . scirmen oððe oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> dema: . . . iddan . . . mæge, ⁊ hi<hi rend="italic">m</hi> wed sellan nelle, gebete mid XXX scill' ⁊ binnan VII nyhtu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> gedo hine ryhtes weorðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="92" ed="#liebermann"/>LII. Gif hwa him ryhtes bidde beforan hwylcum scirmen oððe deman ⁊ him ryht abiddan ne mæge, ⁊ him wedd<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.15"/> syllan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.3"/> nelle, gebete<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.9"/> XXX scll' ⁊ binnon VII nihtum gedó hine rihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="93" ed="#liebermann"/>Be rihtes bene. Gyf hwa him rihtes bidde beforan hwylcu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> scirmen oððe oðru<hi rend="italic">m</hi> deman ⁊ abiddan ne mæge, ⁊ him wed syllan nylle, gebete XXX scill' ⁊ binnon seofen niht gedo hine rihtes wyrðe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="8" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.star"/><pb n="93" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis rectum sibi roget coram aliquo scirmanno<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.20"/> uel alio iudice et habere non possit, et accusatus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.21"/> ei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.22"/> uadium (recti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.23"/>) dare nolit, emendet triginta sol. et infra<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="24" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.24"/> septem noctes faciat ei recti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="25" target="#Ine_8.lnote.oe.25"/> dignum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="38" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be rihtes bene.] Gif hwa him<ptr type="editorNote" n="15" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.15"/> ryhtes bidde beforan hwelcum scírmen oððe oþrum<ptr type="editorNote" n="16" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.16"/> deman ⁊ [him ryht]<ptr type="editorNote" n="17" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.17"/> ábiddan<ptr type="editorNote" n="18" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.18"/> ne mæge, ⁊ him wedd sellan<ptr type="editorNote" n="19" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.19"/> nelle, gebete XXX<ptr type="editorNote" n="20" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.20"/> scill. ⁊ binnan VII nihton gedó hine ryhtes wierðne<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#Ine_8.attnote.fn.21"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="8" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="376" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LII} Gif hwa him ryhtes bidde beforan hwelcu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> scirmen oððe oþrum deman ⁊ ábbidan ne mæge, ⁊ him wedd sellan nelle, gebete xxx sciƚƚ ⁊ binnan vii nihton gedó hine ryhtes wierðne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="93" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn einer sich [sein] Recht fordert vor<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.1"/> irgend einem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.2"/> Amtmann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.3"/> oder einem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.2"/> anderen Richter und [es<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.4"/>] nicht erlangen kann, indem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.5"/> [Verklagter] ihm ein Pfandversprechen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.6"/> [künftiger Urtheilserfüllung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.7"/>] nicht geben will, so büsse dieser [dem König] 30 Schill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.8"/> und mache ihn binnen 7 Nächten der Urtheilserfüllung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_8.lnote.de.9"/> theilhaftig.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone demands [his] right before any official or another judge and cannot obtain [it], because [the accused] will not give him a pledge [of future fulfilment of judgment], let the latter pay [the king] 30 shillings and within 7 nights make him a partaker in the fulfilment of judgment.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="39" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone demands justice<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_8.attnote.n.1"/> in the presence of any ‘shireman<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_8.attnote.n.2"/>’ or of another judge and cannot obtain it, since [the accused] will not give him security, he [the accused] shall pay 30 shillings compensation<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_8.attnote.n.3"/>, and within 7 days do him such justice as he is entitled to.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="401" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone asks for justice in the presence of any official<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_8.whinote.n.1"/> or other judge, and can not obtain it, and [the accused] will not give him a pledge, he [the accused] is to pay 30 shillings compensation, and within seven days make him entitled to justice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="377" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone demands justice before a certain shireman or another judge and he cannot obtain it, nor will [the accused] give him surety, let [the accused] pay 30 shillings and within 7 nights do for him such justice as he is entitled to.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IEw_2-1">I Ew 2.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:App-AGu_1">App AGu 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="196"><label>same fine</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_1-2">II Ew 1.2</ref> <quote>Turning right back to Ine (2 i), we find the 30s fine for obstruction of justice in the local court</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="196"><label>same fine</label> <ref target="clause:Hu_7">Hu 7–7.1</ref> <quote>Turning right back to Ine (2 i), we find the 30s fine for obstruction of justice in the local court</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="377"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Hl_8">Hl 8</ref> <quote>Compare Hloþhere and Eadric §6 [L8].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="280"><ref target="clause:Af_22">Af 22</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="290"><ref target="clause:IIEw_2">II Ew 2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="380"><ref target="clause:App-AGu_1">App AGu 1</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_8.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">[8] <hi rend="italic">Sogenannte App. ad Aelfredi et Guthrumi foedus, s. X. vel XI. composita, nur im Quadr. erhalten (ed. Schmid, Ges. der Angels.</hi> 424) 1: Si quis rectum sibi petat¹ <hi rend="spaced">fieri coram</hi>² <hi rend="spaced">aliquibus</hi> scyre hominibus uel³ <hi rend="spaced">aliis iudicibus</hi> et impetrare non possit, et uadium (<hi rend="spaced">recti</hi>⁴) ei⁵ <hi rend="spaced">pernegetur</hi>, XXX⁶ sol. emendet et intra⁷ VII noctes faciat ei⁸ rectum (ius <hi rend="spaced">publicum</hi>).<lb type="paragraph"/>1) fieri postulet <hi rend="italic">st.</hi> pe. fi. <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi> 2) al. co. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi> 3) et <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi> 4) <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi> 5) pern. ei <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi> 6) emendetur XXX sol. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi> 7) infra <hi rend="italic">Co</hi> 8) <hi rend="italic">nur</hi> ei r. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> ius pu. <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">[8] So-called App. ad Aelfredi et Guthrumi foedus, s. X. vel XI. composita, preserved only in the Quadr. (ed. Schmid, <hi rend="italic">Ges. der Angels.</hi> 424) 1: Si quis rectum sibi petat¹ <hi rend="italic">fieri coram</hi>² <hi rend="italic">aliquibus</hi> scyre hominibus uel³ <hi rend="italic">aliis iudicibus</hi> et impetrare non possit, et uadium (<hi rend="italic">recti</hi>⁴) ei⁵ <hi rend="italic">pernegetur</hi>, XXX⁶ sol. emendet et intra⁷ VII noctes faciat ei⁸ rectum (ius <hi rend="italic">publicum</hi>).<lb type="paragraph"/>1) fieri postulet instead of pe. fi. TMHkBr 2) al. co. Lond 3) et MHkBr 4) lacking in Lond 5) pern. ei TMHkBr 6) emendetur XXX sol. Lond 7) infra Co 8) only ei r. Lond; only ius pu. TMHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_8.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">scyr. <hi rend="italic">RT;</hi> schirem. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">scyr. RT; schirem. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_8.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ei ac. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ei ac. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_8.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eius <hi rend="italic">R; fehlt MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eius R; lacking in MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_8.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">93</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
